"prose": [
{
"from": 160,
"to": 171,
"text": "No product boot-path touchpoint: the product binary is unchanged, so there is no `smoke` entry. The test-plan declares no boot-smoke path list (`rec.py find --doc test-plan` reads none). The harness's own `boot` (`crates/viola-e2e/src/harness/boot.rs`) is touched only on its in-test arm. Its CLI arm keeps an untied supervisor, and its lifecycle (`boot` → `status` → `logs` → `cleanup`) is the CI `test` job's «Harness lifecycle» step, which the CI read (entry 13) covers. No live leg (`inputs#I1` item 3) and no mutation run (item 4). The fake agent's screens are unchanged, and `cli_verify` is in the block anyway, because step 2 lives there. The acceptance needs CI (the exact-cache-hit read, `inputs#I1` item 2, `inputs#I3`), so the operator pass carries pre-push, hygiene, push, the CI read and the cache-hit read. Every test this chunk adds waits through `WITHIN` (12 s), below the mutants kill (15 s) and cargo-mutants' 20 s floor (`tests/contract_lints.rs` `test_deadlines_sit_below_the_nextest_kill_line`, entry 7). No test socket is added. The full integration and E2E suites (entries 8 and 9) are in the block because step 4 moves 44 spawn sites in 24 files: a site spawned on a thread that ends before its child would now be killed there, and only the full suites read every such site."
},
{
"from": 173,
"to": 184,
"text": "Remove-the-guard controls, each implement's one-shot `gate.py control` (never an entry), each fired with `--timeout 600` on the entry filtered to its own cases. 600 s covers the clone's cold build of the filtered binary: the previous chunk read its in-place firings at 47.56 s and its removed firings at 4.4–12.5 s, in the same tool's clone, `doc:2026-11-17-standing-live-rig/plan` §Test Commands. «Holds» means the named case ran and FAILED with no TIMEOUT line; a `timeout` reading reads the control NOT held. - `stamp-hollow` — `tests/support/home.rs`: step 1(a)'s `stamped` and `stamps.json` check replaced by `is_dir()`   alone (today's rule). Case `stamped_home_rebuilds_a_stamp_restored_without_its_files`, on entry 4. - `tied-pdeath` — `tests/support/tied.rs`: the `prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, …)` call removed. Case   `killed_test_leaves_no_piped_wrapper`, on entry 5. Its survivors are killed by `gone_within`'s failure path   (step 3), so the firing leaves nothing running. - `sup-tied` — `crates/viola-e2e/src/harness/boot.rs`: the tied branch's `pre_exec` removed. Case   `killed_test_leaves_no_harness_session`, on entry 6."
},
{
"from": 186,
"to": 187,
"text": "Each filter selects at least one test once its step lands. Entries 3, 5 and 6 read red at baseline because their tests do not stand yet. Entry 4 selects today's two `stamped_home_*` cases."
}
],
